},{"citationId":"c46"},{"citationId":"c47"},{"citationId":"c48"}],"mentionsLeftOut":445,"citations":[{"id":"c1","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_855fd3f62d583391","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":3,"quote":"an LLM-based agent dynamically traverses a graph with nodes representing document elements (e.g., passages, tables) and edges encoding lexical and semantical similarity or structural relation- ships."},{"id":"c2","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_5bc265c54265ad0b","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":52,"quote":"Compared to traditional RAG, GraphRAG offers enhanced explainability through the explicit relationships encoded between nodes in the graph [2]."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_d1c5a844095455cc","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":52,"quote":"Additionally, in graphs exhibiting homophily—where connected nodes tend to share similar attributes—sensitive information can be inferred from neighboring nodes."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_690d7ef285bc963c","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":17,"quote":"• Adjacency matrix: The adjacency matrix is one of the most popular ways to denote a graph."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_690d7ef285bc963c","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":17,"quote":"• Edge list: The edge list represents each edge in the graph, typically in the form of tuples or triples, such as (i, j) or (i, r, j), where i and j are nodes, and r is the relation between nodes i and j."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_690d7ef285bc963c","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":17,"quote":"• Node Sequence: A node sequence transforms a graph into a sequence of nodes in either an irreversible or reversible manner."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_4f6c66daab3d022a","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":24,"quote":"Building a graph can help enhance document classification by leveraging both local and global relationships between words within a single document [538, 259] and by utilizing document-level relationships [518, 461]."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_3b94e2b8589be29c","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":67,"quote":"Simple is effective: The roles of graphs and large lan- guage models in knowledge-graph-based retrieval-augmented generation."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_ded2f7280a7d465a","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":67,"quote":"Simple is effective: The roles of graphs and large lan- guage models in knowledge-graph-based retrieval-augmented generation."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f22af6d01a52a8fb","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":5,"quote":"Subsequently, the retrieval source expanded to in- clude semi-structured data (PDF) and structured data (Knowl- edge Graph, KG) for enhancement."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_5a03cbc1c12462e6","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":10,"quote":"Like these works, HippoRAG shows the potential for synergy between these two technologies, combining the knowledge graph construction abilities of LLMs with the retrieval advantages of structured knowledge for more effective RAG."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_3169c306dc4be0d2","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":2,"quote":"In these cases, encoding the graph with graph encoders such as GNNs before integrating it into generation can help preserve structural nuances [134, 244, 434, 443, 456]."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_6450d43634bcc2d0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"Our novel design first models the neocortex’s ability to process perceptual input by using an LLM to transform a corpus into a schemaless knowledge graph (KG) as our artificial hippocampal index."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_efa9451554fb14fe","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"However, knowl- edge graph construction (KGC) is inherently chal- lenging: the task requires competence in under- standing syntax and semantics to generate a con- sistent, concise, and meaningful knowledge graph."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_fea0e4fdd53cc2f5","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":15,"quote":"Dynamically fused graph network for multi-hop reasoning."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_3bce00605f627143","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":23,"quote":"• GNN-based generator: Some methods use graph neural networks (GNNs) [207] to conduct the generation."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_ceab239fa8621075","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":11,"quote":"AutoKG: Efficient Automated Knowledge Graph Generation for Language Models."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_6caefdf15f202499","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":9,"quote":"Codekgc: Code language model for generative knowledge graph construction."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_46510d19e232344a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"Inspired by this mechanism, HippoRAG allows LLMs to build and leverage a similar graph of associations to tackle knowledge integration tasks."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_034f58fd4faaa1fd","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":10,"quote":"This graph traversal is mainly used in GraphRAG for knowledge and document graphs."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_ba3f7247d56ece0e","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"1 Introduction Knowledge graphs (KGs) (Ji et al., 2021) are a structured representation of knowledge that orga- nizes interconnected information through graph structures, where entities and relations are rep- resented as nodes and edges."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_f8046fa8982a1e8c","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":11,"quote":"Knowledge graph generation from text."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_6940e750d78fc24e","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"of Computer Science, National University of Singapore, 2NUS Smart Systems Institute {bowenzhang, harold}@comp.nus.edu.sg Abstract In this work, we are interested in automated methods for knowledge graph creation (KGC) from input text."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_4e7880c9886117d5","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":2,"quote":"GraphRAG first uses an LLM to construct a knowledge graph, where nodes correspond to key entities in the corpus and edges represent relationships between those entities."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_36f42e6c927e3d4a","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":10,"quote":"Knowledge graph embedding based ques- tion answering."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_bfbda37929aab298","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":16,"quote":"For structured knowledge, the CoK method [106] first extracts facts pertinent to the input query from a knowledge graph, then integrates these facts as hints within the input, enhancing performance in knowledge graph question-answering"},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_b4fed2f43e42c2c0","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":13,"quote":"The recall@10 scores on these datasets were 0.823, 0.663, and 0.818, respectively, indicating the effectiveness of the retriever across different knowledge graph con- texts."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_04f01eaec8c2736a","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":1,"quote":"Graph, by its intrinsic \"nodes connected by edges\" nature, encodes massive heterogeneous and relational information, making it a golden resource for RAG in tremendous real-world applications."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_2428bbb77a4838ab","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":29,"quote":"30 Instruction: Your task is to construct an RDF (Resource Description Framework) graph from the given passages and named entity lists."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_5a89ad6b926c8d84","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":15,"quote":"[421] leverage graph transformers to generate text from knowledge graph."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_45951d5d601df46b","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":12,"quote":"From local to global: A graph rag approach to query-focused summarization."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_347747745d362e3f","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":2,"quote":"Some graph data may even be multimodal (e.g., text-attributed graphs include both structural and textual attributes, and scene graphs combine structures and vision)."},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_4e898d7f26b21f1d","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":13,"quote":"[455] address this by training models to predict the required number of hops for a given query and retrieving the relevant graph content accordingly."},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_8b9b92607399cb42","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":14,"quote":"14 2.5.3 Graph Augmentation Graph augmentation aims to enrich the retrieved graph to either enhance the content or improve the robustness of the generator."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_63b70d30e6c602f7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"On the Knowledge Graph (KG), retrieval granularity includes Entity, Triplet, and sub-Graph."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_647fc5cca4105512","doc